1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,255
White bread, soda, and other refined carbs can spike your blood sugar after a meal, then crash it soon after - repeated spikes like that are linked to growing insulin resistance.

2
00:00:10,575 --> 00:00:11,789
I'm apple cider vinegar.

3
00:00:12,109 --> 00:00:22,587
Arizona State University researchers found my acetic acid can blunt that post-meal surge - people with insulin resistance needed less insulin for a high-carb meal after taking me first.

4
00:00:22,907 --> 00:00:29,911
A follow-up study found a spoonful at bedtime kept waking blood sugar steadier the next morning in adults with type 2 diabetes.

5
00:00:30,231 --> 00:00:35,212
Just dilute me in water - taken straight, I can wear down enamel and irritate your throat.

6
00:00:35,532 --> 00:00:36,955
On diabetes medication?

7
00:00:37,275 --> 00:00:38,572
Check with your doctor first.

8
00:00:38,892 --> 00:00:40,496
I'm not a substitute for treatment.

9
00:00:40,816 --> 00:00:44,430
Exercise and a balanced plate still matter most.
